    "explanation": "In general, fistulas with an external opening\nanteriorly connect to the internal opening by a\nshort, radial tract. Fistulas with an external\nopening posteriorly track in a curvilinear\nfashion to the posterior midline. However,\nexceptions to this rule often occur if an anterior\nexternal opening is greater than 3 cm from the\nanal margin. Such fistulas usually track to the\nposterior midline. This is known as the\nGoodsall's rule.",
